TEST: wifi: ath11k: send extension descriptor frames with index search

Test only. A frame sent through an MSDU extension descriptor was handed to
the firmware, which released it as a plain buffer. Send these frames with
index search on the AST entry of the destination station, as the vendor host
does for a unicast frame, instead of the address search of the vif.

Record the AST index (hw_peer_id) and hash of the peer from the HTT peer map
event in the station when the peer is created, and clear the record when the
station is removed. The TCL command gets search type 1 (index based address
search), address X search enabled, the search index and the low four bits of
the hash as cache set number. A frame whose station has no known index is
refused and sent linear. Module parameter ext_index_search (default on) is
read per frame. The frames sent with index search and those refused are
counted in the soc debugfs statistics, and the index of each station is
logged once.

Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
